= Knowledge object =

Lightweight V2 semantic infobox for the common identity fields used across knowledge pages.

<pre>
{{Knowledge object
 |entity_type=Concept
 |domain=Biology
 |status=Established
 |provenance=V2 public corpus
}}
</pre>

== Explicit identity only ==

Identity fields intentionally have '''no semantic defaults'''. Omitting a parameter displays <code>Not specified</code> and emits no corresponding semantic assertion.

This prevents missing information from silently becoming claims such as <code>Concept</code>, <code>Established</code>, <code>Unspecified</code>, or <code>V2 public corpus</code>.

Repository validation requires instantiated <code>Knowledge object</code> calls to provide explicit <code>entity_type</code>, <code>domain</code>, <code>status</code>, and <code>provenance</code>, and checks controlled values for Entity type, Domain, and Epistemic status.

<code>Module:Structure</code> now performs the same bounded validation at MediaWiki render time. This is a runtime backstop for direct wiki edits, not a second metadata system: valid calls emit nothing extra, while malformed calls produce an explicit validation error and maintenance category.

This template is a baseline identity surface, not the complete BITwiki schema and not a replacement for every historical V1 infobox parameter.

V1's heavily used [[Template:Infobox]] and larger proposed property catalogs are preserved as implementation and design lineage. The live compatibility template is source-controlled beside V2 templates; new V2 knowledge objects should use this template unless a richer stable surface is justified.

Do not add optional dimensions merely to fill an infobox. When they materially improve the knowledge object, use the dedicated properties documented in [[BITwiki:Semantic properties]], including:

* [[Property:Confidence rationale|Confidence rationale]] — why the present evidence supports the stated standing and what would change it;
* [[Property:Review status|Review status]] — what review or verification has actually occurred;
* [[Property:Lifecycle status|Lifecycle status]] — active, superseded, deprecated, archived, or other maintenance state;
* semantic relationships such as [[Property:Implements|Implements]], [[Property:Part of|Part of]], [[Property:Depends on|Depends on]], [[Property:Supports|Supports]], and [[Property:Contradicts|Contradicts]].

== Epistemic status is not a universal verdict ==

The page-level <code>status</code> describes the evidentiary standing of the page's principal descriptive knowledge at the level where that is meaningful. It does not imply that every interpretation, application, mechanism, or theory mentioned on the page has the same standing.

Use claim- or section-level qualification in the prose when a page contains mixed evidence or genuine dispute. Do not manufacture numerical confidence or review status from the page-level label.

See [[BITwiki:Page format]], [[BITwiki:Epistemics]], [[BITwiki:Epistemic status]], [[BITwiki:MediaWiki substrate]], and [[BITwiki:V1 subject and composition migration]].

